sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch10-23> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "No method of perception and analysis, however advanced, can in complete generality recognize all possible regularities and thus tell immediately whether a piece of data can be generated from some simple description, although higher methods could recognize some regularities current methods miss.";
    dc:type "mathematical";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "No method of perception or analysis can recognize all possible regularities";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 10, “Processes of Perception and Analysis”; section “Higher Forms of Perception and Analysis” (from p. 632), p. 633. Scope: all possible methods of perception and analysis"
}
